// basic design is to go all-windows because i use karabiner on mac to make it 96% windowsy, but need
// to pass through ctrl (instead of the usual automap to cmd) because of the built-in vscode terminal.
// so we have to...
//
//   1. unmap default mac keybindings to prevent anything slipping in and confusing the windows side
//   2. map all default windows keybindings (except alt->cmd) to set the mac baseline
//   3. apply all overrides, duplicating entries where alt is used.

